   \[
   65 \text{ lb} = 65 \text{ lb}
   \]

2. **Convert height to inches to inches**:
   \[
   3 \text{ ft} \times 12 \text{ in/ft} + 6 \text{ in} = 36 \text{ in} + 6 \text{ in} = 42 \text{ in}
   \]

3. **Calculate the cross-sectional area (m²)**:
   The cross-sectional area can be calculated using the formula:
   \[
   \text{Cross-sectional area} = 0.6 \times \sqrt{weight \text{ in pounds)} \times \sqrt{height \text{ in inches.}}
   \]
