   \[
   \text{Cross-sectional area} = 0.6 \times \sqrt{65 \text{ in}} \times \sqrt{42 \text{ in}} = 0.6 \times 8.11 \times 4.2 = 0.6 \times 34.45 = 20.85 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Calculate the required amount of the drug**:
   \[
   \text{Daily area} = \text{Density} \times \text{Cross-sectional area} = 17.5 \text{ mg/m}^2 \times 2.085 \text{ m}^2 = 36.18 \text{ mg}
