3CO(g) + O2(g) → 3CO2(g)

We need the standard freeness of formation (ΔS_f) for each reactant and product at 298 K:

ΔS_f(CO(g)) = 2.015 J/K
ΔS_f(O2(g)) = 2.047 J/K
ΔS_f(CO2(g)) = 2.047 J/K

Now, we can calculate the change in entropy (ΔS) for the reaction:

ΔS = [3 * ΔS_f(CO2(g)] - [3 * ΔS_f(CO(g)) + 1 * ΔS_f(O2(g))]

