Total heat released = (2.5 mol) × (-2220 kJ/mol) = -5550 kJ

The negative sign indicates that the reaction is exothermic, meaning heat is released. The magnitude of the negative sign indicates the amount of heat released.

The amount of heat released when 2.5 moles of propane is completely burned is 5550 kJ.
