","1. **Mass of oxygen in the air:**
   \[
   \text{Mass of oxygen} = \text{Mass of air} \times \text{Percentage of oxygen} = 250 \text{ g} \times 0.25 = 62.5 \text{ g}
   \]

2. **Moles of oxygen:**
   \[
   \text{Moles of oxygen} = \frac{\text{Mass of oxygen}}{\text{Molar mass of oxygen}} = \frac{62.5 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} = 1.95 \text{ mol}
   \]

