\[
v^2 = u^2 + 2as
\]

Where:
- \( v \) = final velocity
- \( u \) = initial velocity
- \( a \) = acceleration
- \( s \) = displacement (height in this case)

Since the acceleration due to gravity acts downward (opposite to the direction of motion), we take \( a = -g = -9.8 \, \text{m/s}^2 \).

