   \]
2. The total momentum conservation:
   \[
   \mathbf{p}_i = \mathbf{p}_f + \mathbf{p_f'}
   \]

The four-momentum transfer \( Q \) is the difference between the initial and final four-momenta of the scattered particle (proton in this case):
\[
Q = P_f' - P_i' = (E_f'/c, \mathbf{p}_f') - (m_p/c, \mathbf{0}) = \left( \frac{E_f'}{c} - \frac{m_p}{c} \right), \mathbf{p}_f'
\]
The square of the four-momentum transfer is:
\[
Q^2 = (P_f' - P_i')^2 = (P_f' - P_i')^2 = (E_f'/c - m_p/c)^2 - (\mathbf{p}_f' - \mathbf{0})^2
\]
Substituting \( E_f' = E_i - m_p \), we get:
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_i - m_p}{c} - \frac{m_p}{c} \right)^2 - \left| \mathbf{p}_f' \right|^2 = \left( \frac{E_i - 2m_p}{c} \right)^2 - \left| \mathbf{p}_f' \right|^2
\]
