<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The index of refraction \( n \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum \( c \) to the speed of light in the medium \( v \):  
\[
n = \frac{c}{v}
\]  
Given that the light travels 0.680 times faster in the plastic than in a vacuum, this means:  
\[
v = 0.680 \times c
\]  
Substituting this into the index of refraction formula:  
\[
n = \frac{c}{0.680 \cdot c} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.47
\]  
Thus, the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is \(\boxed{1.47}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

