The maximum change in wavelength occurs when the angle θ is 180 degrees, which means the photon scatels off the electron at a 90° angle relative to the initial direction. In this case, the ratio h/p is given by:

h/p = 1 - (h/λ)

For maximum change, the angle θ = 180 degrees, so the change in wavelength is:

